    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0149" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg141"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.43 Refugees/1766: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-07-27T19:00:00-04:00">July 27, 1939—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>571. For Myron Taylor. Your 1385, July 27, noon.<anchor n="70" xml:id="d114-f1"/>
                    The President authorizes me to let you know that Monday and Tuesday, October 16
                    and 17, may be confirmed as the days upon which he will hold the suggested
                    meeting in Washington.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
